# What must NOT go into the backend image.
#
# NOTE: files the app reads at runtime are deliberately NOT listed here and so
# ARE copied in: all *.py modules, coffee_rust_model.h5, rag_index.pkl,
# facts.json, requirements.txt.

# ── Secrets — never bake into the image (set via `fly secrets set`) ──
.env
.env.*

# ── Version control / editor / dev tooling ──
.git
.gitignore
.vscode/
.agents/
*.log

# ── Python caches and the local virtualenv ──
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
venv/
.venv/

# ── Runtime SQLite DB — lives on the Fly volume, not in the image ──
# (DB_PATH points at /data/kahawa.db in fly.toml). Shipping the local copy
# would risk it shadowing/overwriting real data on first boot.
kahawa.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal

# ── Training image datasets — NOT read at runtime (only train_model.py uses
#    them, via absolute Desktop paths). ~393 MB, excluded to keep the image lean.
coffee___healthy/
coffee___rust/
coffee___red_spider_mite/
new leaves/

# ── RAG source documents — read ONLY by build_rag_index.py (manual). The app
#    loads the pre-built rag_index.pkl at runtime, never these source files.
Knowledge base/

# ── Frontend — this backend is API-only and does not serve static files.
#    (index.html/login.html/signup.html, css/js, service worker, PWA assets.)
*.html
*.css
*.js
js/
sw.js
manifest.json
apple-touch-icon.png
icon-*.png
bg-*.jpg
flower.jpg
leaf.jpg

# ── Security demo material (docs / standalone demos, not part of the API) ──
security_demos/
SECURITY.md
SQL_INJECTION.md

# ── Infra files themselves don't need to be inside the image ──
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
fly.toml
